  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full two-hour set at McCabe’s Guitar Shop in Santa Monica, California, on Saturday, June 30, 2012 [1][3]. This concert, captured by Paul Martinez, is the only available recording of the event and runs for 83 minutes [1]. The setlist features a mix of well-known tracks and deep cuts, including “Balance,” which had not been played in 48 archived shows, and “Island Garden Song,” absent from 35 previous archived performances [1][3]. Notably, the band played “In the Shadow of the Western Hill” and “Noctifer Birmingham,” both of which are the only archived performances of these songs [1][3]. Other rare selections include “For Charles Bronson” and “Alpha Gelida” [1][3]. The show concluded with a five-song encore featuring “Song for an Old Friend,” “No Children,” “Whole Wide World,” “So Desperate,” and “Color in Your Cheeks” [1]. This performance is the 174th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a show at Swedish American Hall on June 28, 2012 [3]. A listener review of this specific recording notes that the song numbering in the player appears incorrect, with numbers seemingly doubled [2].",
